From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rigaz29 <ryanbagas27@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 18:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] art: allow the dual view zygote JIT on the A37 3.10 kernel

CacheOperationsMaySegFault() refuses the zygote JIT on arm64 kernels
older than 3.12, because before db6f41063cbd ("arm64: mm: don't treat
user cache maintenance faults as writes") cache maintenance on a
read-only view could fault. The A37 kernel is 3.10.108 but has that fix,
so zygote64 logged "Zygote memory only works with dual mappings" and
every 64-bit app ran without JIT. The 32-bit zygote was unaffected.

---
 libartbase/base/utils.cc | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libartbase/base/utils.cc b/libartbase/base/utils.cc
--- a/libartbase/base/utils.cc
+++ b/libartbase/base/utils.cc
@@ -167,8 +167,11 @@
   //
   // This behaviour means we should avoid the dual view JIT on the device. This is just
   // an issue when running tests on devices that have an old kernel.
+  //
+  // The OPPO A37 kernel is 3.10.108 but carries that fix, so 3.10 is enough here.
+  // Without this the 64-bit zygote runs with no JIT at all.
   static constexpr int kRequiredMajor = 3;
-  static constexpr int kRequiredMinor = 12;
+  static constexpr int kRequiredMinor = 10;
   struct utsname uts;
   int major, minor;
   if (uname(&uts) != 0 ||
-- 
2.43.0
